0,Oto-Manguean languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oto-Manguean_languages,The Oto-Manguean or Otomanguean languages are a large family comprising several subfamilies of indigenous languages of the Americas.Tenango Otomi.,"Otomi, Tenango",Otomanguean
1,Tenango Otomi – TIPs,https://tips.translation.bible/tip_language/otn/,Tenango Otomi: “earnestly live good” (source: Tenango Otomi Back Translation). Hausa: “character of goodness” (Hausa Common Language Back Translation). Mandarin Chinese: déxíng 德行 or “moral behavior” (Protestant) / yìlì 毅力 or “willpower” (Catholic).,"Otomi, Tenango",Otomanguean
2,"Otomi, Tenango Language (OTN)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/otn/,"Tenango Otomi is a stable indigenous language of Mexico. It belongs to the Otomanguean language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Otomi, Tenango",Otomanguean
